{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154884-combat-ideas","id":1154884,"title":"Combat ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-01T16:49:30-07:00","id":1154884,"title":"Combat ideas","content":"I'm playing a Verbena mage with paradigm : Creation is Innately Divine and Alive and Witchcraft as his practice.<br /> Now, I got Matter 2, Forces 2, Life 2 and Correspondence 2. Beyond obvious uses of Correspondence and Forces to attack from a distance, what other ideas you got that I could use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T02:40:33-07:00","id":1155006,"title":"","content":"Your standart issue verbena kitchen knife may never go dull. Also, you may exel at hitting weak spots of your targets by scanning them for previous injuries or bodily anomalies.<br /> You could also build a decent defensive by enhancing your pagan clothing with matter.<br /> Never run out of kitchen knifes to throw at your enemies, because you can teleport them into your big pockets. Maybe also throw kittens at them... Corr 2, Life 2 makes it possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T05:17:04-07:00","id":1155022,"title":"","content":"For a fight? Well yes your athame will never go dull. Not sure about teleporting knives form your pockets though.<br /> <br /> However you can totally Curse you enemies in a variety of flavours Example: &quot;The shirt will hurt, the thread will string, the stitching will becomes as thorns upon your flesh!&quot; spit in the general direction of your adversary, spill a bit of blood to seal the pact and you can transmute thorns on the inside of whatever the poor bastard is wearing. Rhodedendorums throsn are good for this, very hard to heal and more than a little poisonous. <br /> <br /> Your clothing can be marked upon with a blessing to protect you from harm, a charm to deflect a blow or to turn a hostile knife/bullet into mist.<br /> <br /> You can create an effigy of your foe and ram needles or knives into it and they feel the results<br /> <br /> You can cast blood sodden runes upon the ground and call to the woods and the roots and the sky and summon a swarm of insects to infest and attack your enemies<br /> <br /> Mime and mimic their actions and cause their weapons to decay and rot as you add elements to the witches dance...<br /> <br /> Just to give you a few Paradigm aligned ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T05:48:00-07:00","id":1155026,"title":"","content":"Use Corr 2 to create spacial ripples around yourself that make you harder to hit. M20 lists that each success gives a +1 to the difficulty on attacks made against you. Call on the element of Wind to protect and guide enemies away from you. <br /> <br /> Use Matter 2 to reinforce the pattern of clothing, granting you an armor rating equal to successes. Call upon the power of the earth for strength and resilience.<br /> <br /> Use Corr 2 and Life 2 to create minor wards against living things that give penalties to dice rolls equal to successes scored. Actually you can combine Corr 2 with any of your spheres to create minor wards. Burning sage for protection fits within witchcraft and is a great way to fluff this spell. <br /> <br /> Life 2 to heal yourself. Focus on the pain of your wounds, and the life blood within. There is power in blood, let it heal you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:48:59-07:00","id":1155055,"title":"","content":"If you use a Ward against living things, be sure to add exceptions (yourself, your friends)<br /> <br /> You could combine Matter 2 and Correspondence 2 to create a portable minnor ward against bullets (or steel). You can attach this to an amulet (or to yourself, with Life 2) and should make a small circle arround your body or amulet that would be harder to affect by most conventional weapons (the aforementioned penalties). This would be Coincidental, as you're just adding a little resistance to the bullets/whatever. Of course, you can't use the weapons or materials you're banning.<br /> <br /> Use Matter 2 Correspondence 2 to steal or send away enemy weapons or ammunition.<br /> <br /> Life 2 may allow you to turn any plant into something poisonous, then you can add that poison tou your blade of preference or a projectile (mundane if you have the correct herbs, Life 2 bypasses that need). Of course, you need to be skilled with poisons to do that, but you may use Life/Matter to isolate and spread the poison. You can also increase the chances to hit using Forces, maybe Correspondence, to better guide your blade.<br /> <br /> Forces gives a lot of options as long as there's energy arround.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T07:47:33-07:00","id":1155384,"title":"","content":"Any other ideas? I really appreciate this ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T07:57:14-07:00","id":1155390,"title":"","content":"There's not really a lot of combat specific options for this type of Sphere set up. Most of your abilities are going to be perceptual/investigative type effects, which is useful for before the fight but not really in the middle of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:39:22-07:00","id":1155466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154884-combat-ideas?p=1155384#post1155384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any other ideas? I really appreciate this ones</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, Forces does open options, to what extent they are obvious I don't know. For instance, this has just come to mind:<br /> <br /> Drink the Natural Power:<br /> Use Forces and Matter to &quot;coat&quot; your blade or another weapon in a form of energy that normaly wouldn't &quot;impregnate&quot; it for long. For instance, get your blade close to a fire and get the fire to swirl arround it, this may consume the blade, and won't stick long without Prime to fuel the effect, but it may be enough to increase the power of the weapon for the time. An variation of this could be used when you parry in melee (if you have a ritualy preparated weapon) to grab the force of the enemy weapon and do a stronger counterattack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:51:30-07:00","id":1155516,"title":"","content":"Make a fire tree, a tree that's made of fire. With a combination of Forces, Matter, and Life, it can be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T20:30:40-07:00","id":1155635,"title":"","content":"Creating a pattern requires Prime 2. That being said, Forces 2 ignition along with Matter 2 transformation could be nasty. 'I have this rock in my pocket-it's flammable. Let me light it. . .'' BOOM!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T01:38:44-07:00","id":1155667,"title":"","content":"Corr 2 (+ Matter 2, if the Storyteller requires it) can move items into your pockets from long distances, as discussed. But it can be used for more than an endless supply of knives or bullet magazines. You could pull out a grenade, stick of dynamite, or hunk of plastic explosive. Or, if your tastes run to the more subtle, you can pull out handfuls of caltrops or steel ball bearings, that can injure or trip opponents who walk on them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, instead of putting something there, you can take something away. Teleport away the bullets in a foe's gun, or the knife in his pocket. It might even be coincidental, since the person could have forgotten to load their gun or pack their knife, or could have mis-counted their shots, or had their stuff pick-pocketed off them (a good trick to set up by simply having the character bump into their target beforehand, faking a pick-pocketing). This will definitely require Matter, in order to be able to locate the items on the target's person (and, thus, make those objects count as being in sensory range, the lowest Correspondence threshold there is).<br /> <br /> Matter 2 is also pretty damn fun, if you know what you're doing. Turning enemy bullets from lead to a softer solid (like rubber, cotton, or felt), or the gun-powder into inert sand. Turning bullet-resistant kevlar into easily punctured fabrics or cardboard (but UNDER the outer surface of the vest, so it doesn't look like you did anything). Turning the enemy's clothes or shoes into fragile or heavier materials, in order to compromise the integrity of their garments or restrict their movement. Making the inner parts of a piece of cover into a stronger material, so it better stops weapons fire (at Matter 3, you gain the ability to just alter the properties of the material and give it more Durability and Structure). Turning regular glass into safety glass or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar_glass\" target=\"_blank\">sugar glass</a>, so you don't get hurt from jumping through it. Transmuting sources of water into flammable liquid or acid, or turning air into noxious or flammable fumes (just add match, lighter, or just a spark). Even changing material in the ceiling or overhanging object into weaker substances unable to support the weight of surrounding original material, causing it to break off and fall on people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-04-2017, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T02:59:55-07:00","id":1155677,"title":"","content":"There is no end to the uses of Forces 2.<br /> <br /> Drawing heat from the surrounding environment into the enemy's weapon, burning their hand (or, alternatively, drawing so much heat OUT, it freezes their hand). Drawing heat onto an enemy directly may cause them to suffer heat stroke, blind them with sweat, or force them to disrobe in an attempt to cool off. Draw heat into your own knife, and watch it do extra aggravated damage when it burns flesh. And then, of course, there's the classic from the Order of Hermes Revised Tradition Book, &quot;Betrayal of the Broken Arrow&quot;, which uses Correspondence 1 + Forces 3 to convert all kinetic energy created by igniting the gunpowder in a bullet into heat energy, causing it and all other bullets in the weapon to explode in the enemy's hands. A bit out of reach for your character at the moment, but something to consider for later.<br /> <br /> Manipulating light can obviously render the character invisible, and they have plenty of mystical senses that can compensate for their own eyes not getting light (including an obvious one the designers never considered: mystically sensing <i>light itself</i>, without relying on the eyes). But Forces can also be used to change where one's form seems to be, so the enemy fires in the wrong direction. Light sources can have their illumination diverted entirely, bathing the battlefield in darkness (which, as we've established, is not problem for the mage). Alternatively, the character could bending light in order to shine into their foe's eyes, blinding them with glare (a trick that could even be coincidental, if they have a reflective surface or light source to shine at the enemy). Causing light to shift and coalesce around the enemy's head at random, by contrast, could serve to disorient them.<br /> <br /> Affecting Sound, meanwhile, can also be effective. Sneaking up on people is easy if you muffle the sound of your footsteps, breathing, and clothing. This same principle can create a True silenced weapon, which may even be coincidental with a suppressor (since not everyone knows that &quot;silencers&quot; don't normally make gunshots perfectly silent). By contrast, one can deafen an opponent by directing all the sound of their discharging firearm into their ears. One's voice can be thrown magically to other locations, fooling the enemy into believing one is somewhere different.<br /> <br /> Gravity is fun to play with. While Forces 2 can't increase gravity, it can decrease, deflect, or redirect its pull. Make yourself weightless, or so light that you leap as if on the moon (and can pull off serious Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon moves, like running on treetops or water). Or you could walk on walls or ceilings, or force a foe to fall in those directions unexpectedly. And if an enemy is so weightless they can't run in and attack you, they might as well be defeated for all the good their non-firearm weapons or hand-to-hand fighting ability are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T02:58:36-08:00","id":1156269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154884-combat-ideas?p=1155677#post1155677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manipulating light can obviously render the character invisible, and they have plenty of mystical senses that can compensate for their own eyes not getting light (including an obvious one the designers never considered: mystically sensing <i>light itself</i>, without relying on the eyes). But Forces can also be used to change where one's form seems to be, so the enemy fires in the wrong direction. Light sources can have their illumination diverted entirely, bathing the battlefield in darkness (which, as we've established, is not problem for the mage). Alternatively, the character could bending light in order to shine into their foe's eyes, blinding them with glare (a trick that could even be coincidental, if they have a reflective surface or light source to shine at the enemy). Causing light to shift and coalesce around the enemy's head at random, by contrast, could serve to disorient them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simpler than that. A blindness curse. Light does not reach your target's eyes. Bonus chips for the optional aberrant lensing effect around the black, empty eyesockets..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 11-06-2017, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}